# Manual API Testing Guide — 52 Endpoints (Postman)

> **Base URL**: `http://localhost/clinic_backend/public`
> **Tool**: Postman (or any REST client)

---

## Setup Instructions

1. Open **Postman** and create a new Collection called `Clinic API Tests`
2. Set a **Collection Variable** `base` = `http://localhost/clinic_backend/public`
3. After each login, copy the `access_token` from the response and save it
4. For CSRF-protected endpoints, first call the CSRF token endpoint, then include the token in the `X-CSRF-TOKEN` header

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **CSRF Rule**: Any POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE on tenant endpoints requires the `X-CSRF-TOKEN` header. You must call the CSRF endpoint first **in the same browser/Postman session** (cookies must persist). In Postman, ensure "Automatically follow redirects" and "Send cookies" are ON.

